Note: IMP on ASL/LSR/ROL/ROR means the accumulator form (ASL A etc.), olc shows it as IMP.

Grouped, roughly easiest first:
- Branches (one line each via branch()): BEQ BCS BCC BMI BVS
- Flags: CLC SEC
- Y register: LDY STY INY DEY CPY  (copy LDX/STX/INX/DEX/CMP)
- Compare X: CPX  (same as CMP but with X)
- Logic: AND ORA EOR  (A = A op M, set Z/N)
- Memory inc/dec: INC DEC  (read-modify-write, set Z/N)
- Shifts/rotates: ASL LSR ROL ROR  (accumulator and memory forms, set C/Z/N)
- Arithmetic: ADC SBC  (carry + overflow flag; the trickiest)
- BIT  (Z from A & M, N and V copied from M bits 7 and 6)
- RTI  (pull status then PC; needed once NMI is wired up)


